       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This is double the maximum, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
